{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-grid BFS. It pads the input with a '#' border into one bytearray, builds the visited map with a C-level bytes.translate over the padded grid, and expands frontier lists level by level, returning as soon as E is reached (or -1 when the queue empties). It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The assay baseline is 3.02451 (noise 2.2%), and the translate variant was adopted for a +10% win. I'm resting here: further gains are likely under the 3% win threshold, and the remaining energy goes back to the lineage store.",
